a haze blankets the streets of pekanbaru  city on the island of Sumatra fires have  been burning here in Riau province for  more than a month many started  deliberately by farmers and plantation  companies to clear land for planting  most of the haze is smoke rising from  this land which is flammable peat below  the surface while it looks like the  fires have been put out there  smouldering underground firefighters are  trying to contain the spread but the  annual dry season is making things even  more difficult forced to find water  wherever they can  from creeks rivers and lakes although  schools have been closed for more than a  week market traders in Rio are open but  say the choking haze is bad for business  I'm worried we can't breathe we want a  solution to this problem I wanted to  stop happening every year and it's  causing breathing problems hospitals are  filled with a growing number of patients  I've seen an increase in the number of  patients 30 percent of them have acute  respiratory infections some have asthma  and pneumonia protesters have taken  their frustrations to the governor's  office we want the companies responsible  for the fires to be punished and find a  solution to stop the haze the government  should let volunteers help with  firefighting efforts we also want the  heads of police and the military to step  down president Joko Widodo stressed that  fire prevention is essential he's  calling on the local government to take  more responsibility by boosting  reinforcements of firefighters and  increasing cloud seeding operations to  induce rain we will find out if this is  intentionally organized or just  sporadically done by local people to  open a farm but seeing the massive area  affected we believe it's organized and  thick smog has crossed borders into  Malaysia and Singapore causing  diplomatic disputes with both
 

